# sm_120 Level-2 native: compiler-declared extended-parameter metadata extender
#
# Opt-in (XG_NATIVE_META_EXTEND, presence-based, default off). At the four
# module-load entry points of the shim (cuModuleLoadData{,Ex},
# cuModuleLoadFatBinary, cuLibraryLoadData) the image is copied and, for
# every sm_120 kernel whose EIATTR_PARAM_CBANK declares param_start 0x380
# with a smaller extent, both compiler-written extent records are raised to
# 0x1520 so the window-args relay blob matches the declared c[0x0] param
# extent: EIATTR_CBANK_PARAM_SIZE (nvinfo id 0x19, fmt 3) and the
# EIATTR_PARAM_CBANK param_size (id 0x0a, fmt 4). All other records/sections
# stay byte-identical unless the second knob is also set. Fail-open on every
# anomaly; idempotent.
#
# SECOND OPT-IN XG_NATIVE_META_KPARAM (KPARAM_INFO ordinal growth). Causal
# evidence (build owner's driver-entry control, raw HX4CV3, same installed
# binary, original entry selected): changing only the relay CU_LAUNCH_PARAM
# BUFFER_SIZE from 0x1520 to the original compute size 0x20 at the real
# driver cuLaunchKernel entry makes all 200 queued kernels launch ret 0 and
# the BE complete and exit cleanly (outputs validated); the full-size relay
# fails the first launch with 701 (kv7jHZ, NmlhJN). The declared ordinal
# extent (0x20) is the candidate the driver checks against the buffer.
# With the knob set, legacy EIATTR_KPARAM_INFO records (id 0x17, u16
# size*4+1) are converted in place to the compiler's own large-parameter
# shape EIATTR_KPARAM_INFO_V2 (id 0x45, u16 plain size; attrs high nibble
# cleared: 0xf500 -> 0x0500 pointer, 0xf000 -> 0x0000 scalar; shape from an
# nvcc 12.9 sm_120 specimen with a 0x1520-byte by-value parameter) and the
# max declared ordinal end is grown to cover 0x1520 blob-relative. Record
# count and ordinal order are preserved. Without the knob the KPARAM
# records are left byte-identical and the HAL below falls back to loaded
# param info.
#
# THIRD PIECE - HAL ORIGINAL-ARGUMENT MARSHALING (cuda_command.cpp). The
# grown ordinals must not be observed by host-side copies: the constructor
# deep copy and the window-relay blob build were per-ordinal calls into
# cuXtraGetParamInfo, which after the growth reports the grown size and
# would copy ~5 KiB from the app's own 8-byte argument pointer before any
# relay is adopted. The extender therefore registers each grown kernel's
# ORIGINAL per-ordinal {ordinal, offset, size} layout keyed by the kernel's
# mangled name (section-name scan; ordinal-indexed, density checked), and
# the HAL marshals host-side copies from those ORIGINAL sizes: the
# constructor deep copy (kernelParams form and the param pointers of the
# extra-buffer form), and the window-relay blob fill. Loaded (grown) sizes
# only reach the driver's launch-side blob validation via the relay
# extra map; plain non-relay launches marshal original sizes. The lookup
# is dlsym("XgGetRelayOriginalParams") on the already-loaded shim, so the
# HAL keeps no hard link to the shim; without the shim or without the knob
# it marshals from loaded param info as before. Regression guard: if the
# registered layout disagrees with the loaded param table (count or last
# offset), the HAL falls back to loaded param info and logs a warning.
#
# FOURTH PIECE - NON-RELAY DRIVER-SIDE OVERREAD CLOSURE. Correct original
# host copies are not enough: an ordinary (non-relay) launch lets the
# DRIVER copy per-ordinal at the loaded (grown) sizes. Command-owned
# params (constructor deep copy) now allocate the LOADED (grown) extent,
# zero-filled (calloc), and copy only the ORIGINAL per-ordinal bytes, so
# the driver's grown-extent read lands in zeroed pad inside the
# allocation instead of ~5 KiB past an original-end malloc (this is what
# a plain level-0/1 launch of the 8-byte timer argument would do).
# Plain passthrough launches (app's raw pointers; the CHECK_STREAM
# fallback and the no-XQueue direct launch in shim.cpp) construct an
# owned deep copy when the kernel's ordinal table was grown
# (XgKernelGrown grew-kernel detection); non-grown kernels keep the
# zero-cost passthrough. Preserving original KPARAM metadata for the
# timer instead (do not grow at all) is not implementable at image-patch
# time: the extender cannot know which kernels ride the relay, so
# corridor padding is the chosen smaller measure. True raw passthrough
# remains only for XLaunchKernelEx with a null config (driver rejects
# the null config before any parameter copy) and direct Driver:: calls
# outside the shim's launch entries.
#
# FIFTH PIECE - ACTUAL LOOKUP CLOSURE (build owner raw eluxHm: with the
# export fixed to nm -D T, the BE still misses the layout lookup and the
# relay adoption sees the GROWN params end 0x1520 past the window base
# 0x1500). Two independent failure candidates are closed without
# guessing about driver internals:
# (1) SYMBOL ACQUISITION: the HAL process may hold TWO libcuda.so.1
#     objects (the shim loaded via LD_LIBRARY_PATH and the real driver
#     loaded by full path from the system dirs through
#     Driver::GetSymbol), so the by-name dlopen(RTLD_NOLOAD) handle
#     could resolve the wrong object. The resolver now probes
#     dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, ...) first, which covers the shim under any
#     name/path it was loaded by; the prior by-name handle probes remain
#     as fallback, and the visibility attributes on the header
#     declarations are preserved.
# (2) KERNEL IDENTIFICATION WITHOUT NAMES: a new exported loaded-shape
#     match XgFindRelayOriginalParams identifies the registered ORIGINAL
#     layout from the LOADED layout alone. The meta extend keeps the
#     KPARAM record count and every ordinal offset unchanged and
#     inflates exactly one ordinal's size so its blob-relative end
#     equals 0x1520; a registered entry matches when count/offsets agree
#     and every registered size is <= the loaded size, with zero diffs
#     (no-op) or exactly one strictly-grown ordinal ending exactly at
#     0x1520. Value-identical duplicate registrations (module reloads)
#     are equivalent; differing candidates are ambiguous and refused
#     instead of guessed. This removes the dependency on the exact
#     string cuFuncGetName reports. XgHasRelayLayouts is a cheap gate so
#     corridors skip the param-info enumeration when the knob is off.
#     Constructor and relay adoption materialize the loaded layout
#     first (alloc truth), then marshal from the original layout via
#     the name query first and the shape match second; the shim's
#     passthrough grown-kernel detection uses the same shape match.
# Files (isolated native source tree):
#   platforms/cuda/shim/src/window_meta_extend.cpp            (new)
#   platforms/cuda/shim/include/xsched/cuda/shim/window_meta_extend.h (new)
#   platforms/cuda/shim/src/intercept.cpp                     (4 hooks)
#   platforms/cuda/shim/src/shim.cpp                          (grown-passthrough guard)
#   platforms/cuda/hal/src/common/cuda_command.cpp            (original-layout marshal
#
# Module images may also arrive wrapped in the CUDA runtime fatbin wrapper
# (__fatBinC_Wrapper_t from fatbinary_section.h: magic 0x466243b1, version
# 1, whose data field points at the real container). Static cudart passes
# this wrapper to cuLibraryLoadData and the driver follows wrapper->data
# (root gdb evidence: debug-module-image.log in raw aY3rBY). The extender
# recognizes the wrapper and hands the load call one owned block holding a
# wrapper copy in a 32-byte slot (24 bytes used) whose data field is
# retargeted at the patched nested container copy inside the same block,
# so the driver receives the original wrapper ABI except for the owned
# data pointer; one free of the handed-out wrapper pointer covers both.
# Wrapper versions other than 1 and nested payloads that are neither
# fatbin nor cubin pass through unchanged.
#
# Deployment status (build owner, raw NmlhJN): the wrapper route engages
# in the real run - the four BE logs confirm both extent records raised
# (0x8/0x20 -> 0x1520), an owned wrapper copy 0x20 + nested container
# 0x4818 bytes, a successful module load and binary guardian preparation -
# while the first launch still returns 701 with the relay alone. The
# declared-ordinal-extent knob plus the original-argument marshaling above
# are the response to the HX4CV3 causal evidence; engagement and effect
# are unvalidated until the build owner's run.
#
# Verified CPU-side on the local priority_workload specimen (no GPU): with
# both knobs the extender patches the same six extent bytes as before,
# converts the six legacy KPARAM records to the V2 shape, grows the two
# max-end ordinals (timer ord0 0x8 -> 0x1520, compute ord4 off 0x18
# 0x8 -> 0x1508), registers both kernels' original layouts and answers
# XgGetRelayOriginalParams with ordinal-dense entries; with only
# XG_NATIVE_META_EXTEND records stay byte-identical (6-byte diff) and the
# query returns 0 (HAL fallback). nvdisasm -c and cuobjdump -elf parse the
# patched cubin and patched fatbin. XgFreeExtendedImage reads the
# preceding allocation header, so it is NOT safe for arbitrary foreign
# pointers. Memory-safety scrutiny in the session did not retain a
# valgrind artifact file, so no retained-clean claim is made. After these
# changes the source compiles as g++ -O2 and as
# -O3 -DRELEASE_MODE -DNDEBUG -Wall -Wextra -Werror,
# for both the shim file and the HAL file.
#
# BUILD NOTE: window_meta_extend.cpp enters the shim sources via
# file(GLOB_RECURSE) evaluated at CMAKE CONFIGURE time. A build directory
# configured before the file exists silently omits it (observed: nm -D on
# the installed libshimcuda.so showed undefined XgMetaExtendImage/
# XgFreeExtendedImage and all six workers failed before reaching ready).
# Re-run the cmake configure step, then --build --target install.
#
# Experimental and unintegrated until the build owner tests it; this is an
# sm_120 native actuator port, not an unchanged upstream artifact.
# Apply plain: patch -p1 < xsched-native-meta-extend.patch
# from the source root (level2-build/.output/<native dir>/source).
--- /dev/null
